# YouTube Analysis Component

This component focuses on analyzing YouTube usage and viewing patterns:

## Structure and Main Components
Located in `youtube-knowledge-graph-insights/`, this component includes:
- Analyzer modules in `analyzer/`
- LLM report generation tools in `llm_report_tools/`
- Pattern analysis utilities in `pattern_analysis/`
- User-specific reports in `user_reports/`
- Combined report management in `combined_reports/`

## Key Scripts
- [youtube-knowledge-graph-insights/main.py](mdc:youtube-knowledge-graph-insights/main.py): Entry point for analysis execution
- [youtube-knowledge-graph-insights/youtube_insight_agent.py](mdc:youtube-knowledge-graph-insights/youtube_insight_agent.py): AI agent for generating insights
- [youtube-knowledge-graph-insights/date_range_analysis.py](mdc:youtube-knowledge-graph-insights/date_range_analysis.py): Time-based analysis of viewing patterns
- [youtube-knowledge-graph-insights/combine_reports.py](mdc:youtube-knowledge-graph-insights/combine_reports.py): Combines multiple reports

## Analysis Reports
- Timestamped reports in `analysis_reports/`
- Combined visualizations in `combined_reports/visualizations/`
- User recommendations in `insights/user_recommendations/`

## Data Flow
1. Raw YouTube data is processed by analyzer modules
2. Pattern analysis identifies trends and correlations
3. LLM tools generate natural language insights
4. Reports are generated and stored in timestamped directories
5. Combined reports integrate multiple analysis outputs
6. User-specific recommendations are generated

## Integration Points
- Connects with health data through the data integration components
- Provides insights for the knowledge graph components
- Feeds analysis results to the prompt engineering pipeline
